<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of the Anglo-Saxons</h1><p class="st-meta">886 CE – 927 CE (approx.) · capital Winchester</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The realm created by Alfred the Great and his son Edward, joining Wessex and English Mercia into the direct ancestor of the Kingdom of England.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 886 Alfred occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> and, according to the Chronicle, all the English not under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> submitted to him. His charters began to use the title king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxons</a>, uniting the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-wessex">Kingdom of Wessex</a> with western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mercia">Mercia</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-lord-of-the-mercians">Aethelred</a>, Lord of the Mercians, who married Alfred's daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelflaed">Aethelflaed</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom was defended by burhs and a reorganised army. Alfred issued a law code and sponsored translations of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> works into English. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-elder">Edward the Elder</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelflaed">Aethelflaed</a> reconquered the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danelaw">Danelaw</a>, including the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/five-boroughs-of-the-danelaw">Five Boroughs</a> and Danish <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-east-anglia">East Anglia</a>, between 910 and 920.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelflaed">Aethelflaed</a>'s death Edward absorbed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mercia">Mercia</a> in 918. In 927 his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelstan">Aethelstan</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> and received the submission of northern rulers, becoming the first king of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-england">Kingdom of England</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-the-anglo-saxons.jpg" alt="Kingdom of the Anglo-Saxons" width="320" height="539"><figcaption>Image: Bartholomew, J. G. (John George), 1860-1920 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anglo-Saxon_Heptarchy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>886 CE – 927 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Winchester</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alfred the Great, Edward the Elder, Aethelstan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Anglo-Saxon kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=906&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-anglo-saxons" aria-label="Kingdom of the Anglo-Saxons on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4650 407 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of the Anglo-Saxons lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4970 663L4970 663M4970 663L4962 619M4970 663L4970 663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4970 663h0M4962 619h0M4970 663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4970 663h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4970 663h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Winchester. <a href="/atlas?year=906&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-anglo-saxons">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
